  :adr/body
  "# ADR-2607195300: PostgreSQL startup and query text boundaries

**Status**: accepted
**Date**: 2026-07-19

## Decision

PostgreSQL StartupMessage user and database values are non-empty, at most 63
bytes and contain no NUL. Simple Query text is non-empty, at most 65,535 bytes
and contains no NUL. Startup fields are checked before opening a transport;
query text is checked before writing a frame. This prevents a component from
injecting additional NUL-terminated startup parameters or silently truncating
a query at the wire boundary.

## Maturity boundary

These are protocol framing limits, not SQL authorization. Query semantics,
role privileges, row-level security and transaction policy remain the database
server or a higher-level capability provider's responsibility."}]
